//------------------------------------------------
//--- 010 Editor v8.0 Binary Template
//
//      File: MP4.bt
//   Authors: Alexey Lyashko, Andrew Molyneux, Marian Denes, SweetScape, Marko Musa
//   Version: 3.3
//   Purpose: Defines a template for parsing MP4 and MOV video files.
//  Category: Video
// File Mask: *.mp4,*.mov,*.m4v
//  ID Bytes: [+4] 66 74 79 70, [+4] 6D 6F 6F 76, [+4] 6D 64 61 74
//   History:
//   3.3   2019-08-08 M. Musa: Modified box logic to respect box size in header.
//   3.2   2019-02-03 A. Lyashko: Added support for fragmented MP4 files.
//   3.1   2018-06-17 A. Lyashko: Added support for sample table atoms.
//   3.0   2017-10-03 A Molyneux: Total rewrite, more complete and robust.
//   2.2   2016-01-29 SweetScape: Updated header for repository submission.
//   2.1   2015-06-04 M Denes: Public release.
//------------------------------------------------
//
// REWRITE NOTE -- generative rewrite driven by
//   llm_learned_specification/opus5-tiered/llm_reterived_constraints_mp4-llm_opus5-tiered.json
//
// TIER DISCIPLINE
//   Tier A fields carry their computed value inside a SetEvilBit(IsParsing()) guard.
//   IsParsing() is false while generating, so no Tier A field ever takes FormatFuzzer's
//   1/128 out-of-set "evil" value; it is true while parsing, which is the only thing
//   that lets a computed field accept a real file's own bytes (a literal
//   SetEvilBit(false) makes the template reject every real file).
//   Tier B fields carry their complete valid_values set, weighted by preferred_value.
//   Tier C fields are declared bare: no value set, no <min=>, no <max=>.  There is not
//   one min/max attribute in this file.
//
// PLAN-THEN-EMIT, AND WHY THE BOX SIZES ARE BACKPATCHED
//   boxheader.size is the stride to the next box and the bound of every container walk,
//   so a generator cannot write it until the box body is finished.  Every box therefore
//   emits a placeholder size, runs its body, and then seeks back and writes the real
//   total (boxheader.size / boxheader.size64, calculated_value).  Container bodies are
//   driven generator-side by a planned child list instead of by the placeholder, because
//   the original's "while (FTell() < endOffset)" cannot run against a size that is not
//   known yet.  The parse direction keeps the original's loop exactly.
//
// THE CHUNK OFFSETS ARE THE LAST THING WRITTEN
//   mp4box.chunk_offset is an ABSOLUTE file offset into the mdat box, so it cannot be
//   written until both moov and mdat have been laid out.  The generator records the file
//   position of every offset slot it writes, together with that chunk's byte offset
//   inside the mdat body, and rewrites them all once the mdat body position is known.
//   That is what makes moov-before-mdat and mdat-before-moov both expressible
//   (structure rule 5) without pinning the layout.
//
// WHAT THE SAMPLE ENTRIES ARE FOR
//   The stsd sample entry is the one measured gate in this format that stops stream
//   creation outright.  Five sample-entry emitters are written, each framed exactly as
//   ISO/IEC 14496-12 requires -- declared size, six zero reserved bytes, a non-zero
//   data_reference_index, and the codec configuration box nested inside the declared
//   size -- while everything inside them stays free.  Of those, two produce media a
//   decoder can actually consume: an uncompressed QuickTime video entry whose samples
//   are exactly width*height*bytes_per_pixel, and uncompressed PCM audio.  The
//   geometry written into a sample entry is payload content, which the JSON records as
//   free; the track geometry in tkhd is a Tier C field and stays bare.
//
// OUTPUT BUDGET
//   structure rules 1, 3, 4, 6, 7 and 8 give byte budgets of 1 MiB for the file, 768 KiB
//   of media data, 256 KiB of moov, 16 KiB of sample descriptions, 64 KiB of free and
//   unregistered boxes and 128 KiB of movie fragments.  This runtime's MAX_FILE_SIZE is
//   65536, so each is scaled by the same factor and drawn per file from a broad
//   distribution.  A second counter estimates MAX_RAND_SIZE consumption.  No dimension,
//   timescale, sample count, entry count or repetition field is ever capped to fit --
//   the generator spends the budget by ending the sample sequence.
//
// INDEPENDENCE
//   Written from templates_originals/mp4-orig.bt and the tiered constraints JSON only.
//------------------------------------------------

BigEndian();

struct fp16;
struct fp32;
struct fp32uvw;
struct matrix;
struct fourcc;
struct boxheader;
struct compatible_brand;
struct mp4box;
struct mp4time;
struct mp4lang;
struct qtopcolor;
struct elst_entry;
struct tkhd_flags;
struct vmhd_flags;

